## Lore

The Akysse are tribal hunters of the swamps and forests along the eastern
seaboard, from old Virginia south through the Carolinas, Georgia and
Florida, and they have lived that way on Rifts Earth for nearly three
centuries. They are orange-skinned humanoids with backward-bending legs,
three-fingered hands, a short tapir-like snout, pig-like ears and a finned,
red-striped crest on the head that keeps them cool. Neighbors call them
Red Capped Wild Men or Pig Barbarians.

They follow the great herds - dinosaurs, Rhino-Buffalo, Fury Beetles -
sleeping under the sky or in hide tents and dressing in loincloths and
patchwork armor of M.D.C. bone and hide. The men hunt and guard the clan;
the women gather and raise the young. They bring down huge beasts with
Vibro-Blades and other melee weapons taken from travelers and from the
slavers who hunt them, but they are hunters rather than soldiers, and their
tactics are surprise, ferocity and numbers.

Akysse distrust outsiders and technology, and they bury, smash or drown any
gun or gadget they capture. They speak Gobblely among themselves and treat
anyone who does not as a stranger. They do not hold grudges, but settlers
who try to put down roots in their lands are driven off, and slavers are
hated above all; an Akysse will fight to the death to free a captive.

## GM Notes

Starting money: the book prints 1D6x1,000 credits worth of tradable goods, not coin, so no starting_money is stored (money is coin only).

Size 5 to 6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 m). Weight 100-200 pounds (45 to 90 kg). Life
span 2D6+50 years.

Experience Level (NPC): 1D4+3, or as set by the Game Master.

Standard equipment the catalog has no row for: a Vibro-Spear made by lashing
one or two Vibro-Knives or a Vibro-Saber to a pole (1D6, 2D4 or 2D6 M.D.), a
suit of patchwork Fury Beetle or dinosaur hide armor (4D6+28 M.D.C.), a
medicine pouch, a water skin, three loincloths, and 1D4 dinosaur and animal
calls. With a Horsemanship skill the character may start with a good riding
horse, or with Horsemanship: Exotic a small predatory dinosaur such as a
Silonar or Ostrosaurus, at the G.M.''s discretion.

Habitat: the temperate forests, low mountains and swamps of the Southeast,
moving north only in summer. Clans run from five to 500 members, usually
under 100; one of 3,000 or more is rumored in the Georgia Piedmont or the
Florida Panhandle. Fewer than 15,000 in all.

Slave Market Value: twice an average human, prized for the arenas.

Allies: only their own clan. Rogue and exiled Akysse get on well with
humans and D-Bees. Psi-Goblins, Goblins and Orcs are generally accepted.
Enemies: Tech-Invaders, rival tribes, and above all the Splugorth and their
minions. They avoid Shemarrians, sensing something is wrong with them.
